{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"90792dd3-0417-498d-b1c1-3db8937584c4","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Flip a fair coin twice. The first flip branches into heads or tails, each with probability one half.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Two fair coin flips"},{"op":"figure","id":"tree","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.5,5.8],"y":[-2.7,2.7],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"start","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"head","at":[2,1.3],"label":"H"},{"kind":"point","id":"tail","at":[2,-1.3],"label":"T"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"start"},"to":{"at":"head"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"start"},"to":{"at":"tail"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"text","at":[1.1,2.4],"text":"First flip","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"fair","region":"A2","latex":"P(H)=P(T)=\\frac12"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"90792dd3-0417-498d-b1c1-3db8937584c4","step":{"id":"s2","script":"From either first result, the second coin again gives heads or tails. Follow each complete path to list the four possible outcomes.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"branches","on":"tree","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"hh","at":[4,2]},{"kind":"point","id":"ht","at":[4,0.6]},{"kind":"point","id":"th","at":[4,-0.6]},{"kind":"point","id":"tt","at":[4,-2]},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"head"},"to":{"at":"hh"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"head"},"to":{"at":"ht"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"tail"},"to":{"at":"th"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"tail"},"to":{"at":"tt"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"text","at":[4.6,2],"text":"HH"},{"kind":"text","at":[4.6,0.6],"text":"HT"},{"kind":"text","at":[4.6,-0.6],"text":"TH"},{"kind":"text","at":[4.6,-2],"text":"TT"},{"kind":"text","at":[3.8,2.4],"text":"Second flip","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"path","anchor":{"el":"fair","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(HT)=\\frac12\\times\\frac12=\\frac14"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which outcomes have exactly one head, and what is their combined probability?","expected_gist":"HT and TH; each has probability 1/4, so their combined probability is 1/2."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"90792dd3-0417-498d-b1c1-3db8937584c4","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Multiply along a path, then add the paths you want. Exactly one head means HT or TH: two quarters make one half.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"selected","on":"tree","marks":[{"kind":"circle","center":[4.6,0.6],"r":0.35},{"kind":"circle","center":[4.6,-0.6],"r":0.35},{"kind":"text","at":[5.3,0.6],"text":"1/4","size":"small"},{"kind":"text","at":[5.3,-0.6],"text":"1/4","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"answer","anchor":{"el":"path","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\text{exactly one head})=\\frac14+\\frac14=\\frac12"},{"op":"text","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"answer","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Multiply along; add across."}],"checkpoint":null}}
